{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And they brought their offering, a fire-offering to YHWH, and their sin-offering before YHWH.</b> The Ramban, z\"l, wrote: this is like what they said, 'He and His court.' He said that they brought their offering to the specific Name, and their sin-offering before Him — now, the sin is atoned through the attribute of mercy and through the attribute of judgment, and He mentioned this in connection with idolatry. And He mentioned ״ולגר הגר בתוכם״, because the converts are always tripped up by this sin. End quote. The explanation of his words: לפני ה' in most places means the attribute of judgment alone, whereas לפני ה' as it appears here — the intent therein is only 'He and His court.' And Scripture says: והם הביאו את קרבנם. אשה לה' — that is the supernal Name, the place of the עולה; and their sin-offering they brought לפניו, that is, to His face — which is He and His court. And ונסלח is mentioned twice, because the sin is atoned through the attribute of mercy and the attribute of judgment. And the language of שגגה is mentioned at the beginning and at the end, and likewise at the beginning of the parashah and at its end, to say that it is fitting to forgive them, since they brought their offering as an עולה and fulfilled their obligation in full — for it was after all a שגגה."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:39.742532285Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}